  "findings": [
    "All eight still pairs tied overall and every image was usable. Likeness alone favored 1K twice, 0.5K once, with five ties.",
    "0.5K-derived videos won overall three times with five ties and no losses; usable 8/8 versus 1K 6/8.",
    "All four portrait-video pairs tied on all rated axes and all were usable. Both rejected 1K videos were uploaded Oyster bodies; one note reports face distortion.",
    "Both takes of the uploaded Celery body were usable at both resolutions. 0.5K won overall once and tied once.",
    "Resolution won speed in seven of eight matched image cases; median paired image saving and cold image+video saving were each about 2.9 seconds.",
    "Small two-identity, two-take study; do not infer that lower resolution inherently improves video quality. Earlier four-pair still sweep favored 1K three times, so still-image superiority is not settled."
  ],
  "scope": "Two identities, four cases, two takes per case. Portrait and full-body production routes differ. Shared still/video outputs are related. Body videos retain choreography references; results cannot prove equivalence on the no-reference path. Cold image+video request sum excludes planning and common uploads/downloads.",
  "productionChanged": false
}